    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d450">

                <pb facs="0628" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">660P.116/29b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Latvia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Cole</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-02-06T17:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Department’s No. 55, December 5, 1934, 5 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d450-f1"/>
                    Please expedite submission of desired report which should show definitely
                    whether American trade is now receiving most-favored-nation treatment in Latvia
                    and, if not, precisely wherein such treatment is being denied. Department is
                    requesting by cable similar report from Legation at Kaunas to which you should
                    forward copy of Tallinn report No. 43<anchor n="3" xml:id="d450-f2"/> to serve
                    as model.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
